   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Ground_%28Walter_Trout_album%29",
   "resumo_en": "Common Ground is the 11th studio album by American blues rock musician Walter Trout. Recorded in March 2010 at House of Blues Studios in Encino, Los Angeles, it was produced by John Porter and released on July 6, 2010, by Provogue Records. Like Trout's previous album The Outsider, which was also produced by Porter, Common Ground features session musicians James \"Hutch\" Hutchinson (on bass), Kenny Aronoff (on drums) and Jon Cleary (on keyboards) – his regular band members are not featured. The album reached number 6 on the US Billboard Blues Albums chart and number 13 on the UK Jazz & Blues Albums Chart.",
